  "body": "Slice 1 refuses --kind/--topic/--project/--client/--since/--until on the shard path (loudly) because scan shards carry no sessions/labels, and keeps keyword (FTS) search on the libSQL monolith (TursoDB MVCC shards have no chunks_fts). Decide: session-label filters resolved via content store ids pushed into the scan, vs. staying on the monolith until cutover; and a dedicated FTS store or monolith-until-cutover for keyword search. Refs #5755, #5669.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- A decision is recorded on this issue: session-label filters via content-store ids pushed into the scan, or monolith-until-cutover — with the reasoning.\n- Keyword/FTS search has a decided home (dedicated FTS store or monolith-until-cutover) recorded the same way.\n- Whichever path is chosen, the shard consumer no longer silently lacks --kind/--topic/--project/--client/--since/--until or FTS behaviour: it either supports them or refuses them loudly with the decision linked.\n",
